Fairly straightforward.  The intro chords/riffs are used throughout
the song.  Each period (in the chord-thing) below represents one
measure (one play-through of each riff above).  So, you'd play A
four times, E four times (the fourth time play the transition), D
four times, and then A twice and E twice.  That's it.  Probably the
most important thing to remember is to accent the third beat of each
measure (which is the added 6th of each chord).  Just listen along
and you'll get the idea.

